WEBVTT

00:00:00.256 --> 00:00:03.821
Under Configure, open Enable Data-at-Rest Encryption.

00:00:04.096 --> 00:00:08.513
Choose PE direct and enter the expected cluster UUID, PE

00:00:08.533 --> 00:00:10.985
endpoint and saved credential reference.

00:00:11.087 --> 00:00:15.014
This path uses Prism Element and an existing Local KMS;

00:00:15.055 --> 00:00:18.363
it does not require Prism Central or SSH.

00:00:18.553 --> 00:00:21.499
It is not an external key-manager conversion tool.

00:00:21.711 --> 00:00:26.308
New deployment and recovery drafts offer optional PE certificate verification.

00:00:26.549 --> 00:00:31.031
A per-run exception needs an explicit reason, independent approval and

00:00:31.071 --> 00:00:35.617
an audit record. HTTPS remains encrypted, but bypassing

00:00:35.637 --> 00:00:39.660
certificate verification removes that certificate-based identity check.

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:44.086
The exception applies to this operation and does not change global trust or other

00:00:44.106 --> 00:00:46.916
workflows. Run read-only discovery.

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:50.983
Verify cluster identity, complete healthy membership, supported

00:00:51.003 --> 00:00:54.418
software-encryption state and the reported Local KMS.

00:00:54.544 --> 00:00:58.705
Review licensing, platform support, other encryption tasks and

00:00:58.725 --> 00:01:03.199
key-backup ownership. Missing, partial or unsupported states block

00:01:03.219 --> 00:01:06.023
the operation rather than being converted automatically.

00:01:06.377 --> 00:01:09.664
Software encryption cannot be disabled after enablement.

00:01:09.876 --> 00:01:13.898
Review the exact plan and obtain approval from a different administrator.

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:18.324
Packaged appliances enable reviewed live application by default, while an

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:21.268
explicit host override can retain planning mode.

00:01:21.458 --> 00:01:23.971
Validate the installed version and hardware.

00:01:24.133 --> 00:01:28.700
Before submission, the exact confirmation precedes fresh identity, health

00:01:28.826 --> 00:01:30.833
and state checks and one request.

00:01:31.215 --> 00:01:35.547
PE configuration readback and background
encryption monitoring are separate from

00:01:35.567 --> 00:01:37.393
proof that keys can be recovered.

00:01:37.594 --> 00:01:41.073
Preserve and verify key backups outside the appliance.

00:01:41.348 --> 00:01:45.723
If submission or verification is uncertain, inspect actual PE state

00:01:45.743 --> 00:01:49.841
before another request. Rolling back the Orchestrator does not turn encryption

00:01:49.924 --> 00:01:50.460
off.
